## Metric definitions

Definitions live in `.ai_context/knowledge/metrics.md` (create on first
metric). A number without a pinned definition is not a result.

## Definition of done

- Numbers are **reproducible**: fixed data window, pinned parameters/seed,
  and the exact command recorded next to the result.
- No lookahead / survivorship bias in the data path — state how you checked.
- Limitations and data-quality caveats stated alongside the findings.
- Every reported number passed `/number-check`: work count (trades /
  rows), quiet-failure count (errors / NaN), run or window spread, and
  the limiter stated with it.
- Findings dated into `.ai_context/journal/`; stable conclusions promoted
  to `knowledge/`.

## Project rules

<!-- Only deviations from global defaults. Keep short. -->

- _(none yet)_

## Memory & mechanisms

- `.ai_context/` is the project's persistent memory; `INDEX.md` is the
  authority for what lives where.
- Run `/wrap` at session end.

## Long-horizon tasks

- Multi-stage pipeline work (> ~30 min autonomous) goes through
  `/task <description>` — lanes run a real pipeline slice (one day / one
  symbol / one cohort), print its row count as an `expect` marker and go
  red on a broken input (the canary); zero rows processed is unproven.
- Work happens on a `task/<slug>` branch from a clean tree; a slice is done
  only when `bash scripts/evidence.sh done S<n>` accepts it.
